  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $7.25$ | $8.5$ | $9.25$ | $5.75$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(3) & \u2248\\frac{g(3+1)-g(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(3)}{1} \\\\  & =2.5-5.75 \\\\  & =-3.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
